@ssahani @yuwata I reworked this and I think is better now.

The first 2 patches I believe are safe, and only delay continued configuration until after confirmation that the genmode has been set, although I am not 100% certain if the netlink handler is single-threaded; if both the MTU and genmode are set, then there may be a race condition there where both the mtu and genmode handler functions could call link_configure_continue() - but it seemed like the netlink processing runs callbacks single-threaded, so I think that can't happen, right?

The last patch moves the link_drop_foreign_config() call to later in configuration, and while I think this is safe, it's the part I was least certain about.  Is there anything during link_configure() that expects foreign config to be dropped, or that would break if foreign config is dropped later?

@ssahani I have a question about the networkd tests, which isn't directly related to this, but I included some updates to test/test-network in this PR so I'll just ask here...there is a test/networkd-test.py created by @martinpitt that doesn't appear to be updated much anymore, and then also the newer test/test-network/ tests that you created; do we need to keep them separate still, or is it ok if I transfer the tests in test/networkd-test.py into test/test-network/?  also @yuwata ^

The Ubuntu CI doesn't currently run the new test/test-network tests, which I'd like to fix:
https://salsa.debian.org/systemd-team/systemd/merge_requests/58
@mbiebl pointed out we don't need 2 separate networkd test suites and should merge them, which I agree with

