@ssahani re: netdev_enslave_ready, one thing I thought about was the situation where networkd is configured to manage a VLAN interface, but is not configured to manage the VLAN's corresponding physical interface.

In that case, I don't think there is any way that networkd could guarantee the VLAN interface would not come up during setup (and experience this problem); networkd might not even know the interface is a VLAN, e.g. if the VLAN is created by something else but managed by networkd.

I think I can rework the merge request to keep using netlink to set the addr_gen_mode, if that is your main concern - I think the only 2 things really required are 1) networkd itself shouldn't bring up the interface until after we get a netlink response indicating addr_gen_mode has been set, and 2) right after we have confirmation addr_gen_mode is set, we should check for existing tentative addresses, and drop them.  Does that sound more reasonable?

